 CellLabel->
  "Out[4]//TableForm=",ExpressionUUID->"d22f8398-f015-4466-a71b-db7a5348dae3"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We see there is a single Pi group (meaning it is a constant), which we can \
write as either V = c ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["R", "3"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "6783ff40-2d35-4ab7-837c-378652286d25"],
 " or R = b ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["V", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "3"}]], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "d1793833-49b2-48f8-8af9-d4088da0eb4f"],
 ".  Everyone knows from Calculus that c = 4/3 \[Pi], and this cannot be \
determined from dimensional analysis alone.  However, if we do the \
dimensional analysis, we could determine the constant from a single \
experiment where we measure the radius and volume of a sphere!\n\nThe \
different versions of the Pi groups are chosen according to the simple \
criteria that each group isolates one of the input variables, and reports it \
as raised to the first power.  In this case there are two such groups.  \n\n\
Suppose we hypothesize that the volume of an ellipsoid, V, is related to the \
lengths of the 3 semi-axes, a,b, and c."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9374119436936207`*^9, 3.937411963911318*^9}, {
  3.9374120486479893`*^9, 3.937412111404607*^9}, {3.937412151767913*^9, 
  3.937412300035787*^9}, {3.93741233854494*^9, 3.93741234489017*^9}, {
  3.937413439194235*^9, 3.937413454951344*^9}, {3.937413837766567*^9, 
  3.9374139283624573`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c0da2cef-25da-4bc7-8aee-\
a6aa557647d8"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"vars2", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"V", ",", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Meters\>\"", "^", "3"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"a", ",", "\"\<Meters\>\""}], "}"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"b", ",", "\"\<Meters\>\""}], "}"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"c", ",", "\"\<Meters\>\""}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9374053065827513`*^9, 3.9374054378270893`*^9}, {
  3.937405507488226*^9, 3.937405553732486*^9}, {3.937411967822328*^9, 
