Cell["\<\
Finally, since we in general do not know how many variables we can specify, \
BuckPi will ignore the trailing members of the list that cannot have unity \
power.  For example, there is not valid set of Pi groups that only involve \
all variables raised to the first power (in this example).  \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9374126656979523`*^9, 3.937412705149478*^9}, {
  3.937412742185204*^9, 
  3.9374128318857117`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8e486ac6-7256-48e1-8251-\
1e9a66f01899"],

