Cell["\<\
We see that none of the Pi groups involve the density, since there is nothing \
to cancel its mass units in any of the other quantities.  Thus it is not \
possible for the phase speed to depend on the density unless it also depends \
on some other quantity involve mass units (such as the surface tension).  If \
surface tension is unimportant, then there are just 2 Pi groups and density \
is likewise unimportant.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9374136834374228`*^9, 
  3.9374137632998867`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1703de2b-063a-45e6-b40c-\
23d754295356"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
},
